@cc [owner:pmilliotte,label:error-handling;api] sdk-throws-typed-errors
This package is the runtime SDK linked into Frame and Pod function code, not repository code: its
exported functions MAY throw expected failures, as an exception to `no-catching-own-errors`. A
thrown expected failure MUST be an instance of an exported `Error` subclass that sets `name`, so a
function author can branch on it with `instanceof`. Code in this package MUST NOT catch an expected
failure raised by another function of this package. This exception covers failures raised by this
package only; repository code elsewhere, including the functions runner and front, stays governed
by `no-catching-own-errors`.

@cc [owner:pmilliotte,label:error-handling;api] sdk-documents-thrown-errors
Every exported function of this package that can throw an expected failure MUST carry an `@throws`
line naming the error class and the condition that raises it, on its own documentation comment or,
when the failure applies to all methods of an exported object, on that object's documentation
comment. A failure that is not documented this way is not covered by `sdk-throws-typed-errors` and
MUST be returned rather than thrown.
